{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1069607-gnosis-3-or-10-merit-points","id":1069607,"title":"Gnosis 3 or 10 Merit Points?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-28T14:03:13-07:00","id":1069607,"title":"Gnosis 3 or 10 Merit Points?","content":"Inspired by another thread, should you chose 10 merits or Gnosis 3 at character creation.<br /> <br /> <b>In favor of Gnosis 3:</b><br /> <br /> You get a second obsession, meaning you generate Arcane beats from obsessions twice as fast as a character with lower gnosis. Figure this is an advantage of around 1 Arcane beat a game.<br /> <br /> You get two extra Praxis. Criting a praxis means that you can selection a condition that resolves for a beat. Figure this is worth at least 1 beat a game.<br /> <br /> So, give or take Gnosis 3 means one extra XP per two game sessions.<br /> <br /> You qualify to join (or found) a legacy immediately out of character creation. The Gnosis 1 character will need to buy up Gnosis to 2 to join an established legacy.<br /> <br /> Many of the most interesting merits can be purchased by individual dots. A characters first 5xp are probably going into Shadow Name (3), Themed Cabal (1) and the first Legacy Attainment. You can buy these dots as you go. The Gnosis 1 mage needs to save up 5xp and then gets a big power boost all in one go. For a game that does not run for many sessions, this can mean that a character is making major purchases just as the game is wrapping.<br /> <br /> Extra maintained spell slots give the mage the ability to have a mix and match template. For example, with Life 3, and pushing things pretty much to their limit, you can generate around 7 to 8 bonus attribute dots on a one month ritual or gain healing at about the same speed as the base level of a werewolf, with Armor 8 to boot.<br /> <br /> You can combine spells, which can be handy for two relatively low powered merit boosters.<br /> <br /> It takes six hours, instead of 18 hours -- to cast a ritual spell with a +5 dice time bonus.<br /> <br /> You have an extra Yantra slot. If you can work in a +2 Yantra this means that (+2 Yantra +2 Gnosis) you pull even with a character that spend 4 merit points on Shadow Name 3 and themed Cabal (though honesty, Themed cabal should be everyone's first in game purchase).<br /> <br /> Magic can provide merit's but it's limited. RaW say that Arcana 2 is sufficient to generate merit dots, but that any merits that apply a dice pool effect apply it only as many times as the spells potency. Fate can generate Resources, Contacts (I think Allies), Retainer and probably one or two others I'm not remembering. Life can provide most physical merits. Mind most knowledge based ones (which I would assume includes fighting styles). Time can rewrite history. In addition, though it's tempting the SG, you can use magic simply to generate merits that are not paid for and not protected in game (for example using matter to repair big rig cabs for resale). Other Arcana can also be used to generate merits. While somewhat limited, it might be more efficient to cast a potency 5 spell when you need to make a resources 5 purchase than to have a static resources of 5 (though perhaps you should pair with time 1 to make sure you know what form the luck involved in gaining those resources will take)..<br /> <br /> <b>In favor of 10 merit points:</b><br /> <br /> For the most part, magic cannot provide the more powerful merits like order status or the various order merits. (Perhaps Prime 2 might be able to create a temporary Shadow Name).<br /> <br /> For five dots (Safe Place 1, Sanctum 1, Soul Stone +3), you can start with a Sanctum that has a demense. This greatly helps with both summonging and long duration ritual spells (no paradox).<br /> <br /> A number of those merits provide either additional or mix and match merits in some way. A character who is pushing the rules (using mystery cult influence to generate a shadow name) and has mystery cult influence at 5 and status or profession training at 5 has the equivalent of 20xp worth of merits. That's very front loaded<br /> <br /> You can create a character with a cool mundane identity, for example an awakened international assassin.using professional training. <br /> <br /> You can rearrange merit dots with time to create alternative identities.<br /> <br /> You generate less paradox.<br /> <br /> In situations where you have to cast a non-rote spell in a single turn, a mage with +3 Shadow Name +1 themed cabal has up to a +2 dice advantage over a higher gnosis mage without Shadow name advantages.<br /> <br /> <b>Logic:</b><br /> <br /> Low Gnosis mage is front loaded by buying &quot;advanced&quot; merits that give the benefit of 2 standard merit points per each merit point put into it (literally for mystery cult and some others). If low gnosis mage has to prioritize getting gnosis to 3 then high gnosis mage will pull even as soon as high gnosis mage accumulates 10 xp. Assuming high gnosis mage is getting 2xp per session, this should take place around session 5. Assuming low gnosis mage only gets 1.5 xp per session it will take 7 sessions to buy up Gnosis to 3. <br /> <br /> Low gnosis mages are likely to be slightly ahead of the power curve for the first couple game sessions and slightly behind it thereafter.<br /> <br /> At about sessions 7 you would have one mage with: Gnosis 3, Status 4 (3+1), Shadow Name 3, Mystery Cult Influence 4 (Resources 3, Skill point +1, Contacts 2) and Themed Cabal 1 (obligatory session one buy.<br /> <br /> At the same time you would have a high Gnosis Mage with. Gnosis 3, Themed Cabal 1, Shadow Name 3, Legacy Attainment 1, One Ruling Arcana at 4, Mystery Cult Influence 3 (+1 skill dot, Resources 2) and +2 rotes/praxis (or possibly status 3 or just 2xp banked towards raising Gnosis to 4)<br /> <br /> The adept is probably to more powerful character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12994-steveintexas","name":"SteveInTexas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T14:13:05-07:00","id":1069612,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that some Merits can only be bought at character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T14:24:21-07:00","id":1069621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SteveInTexas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1069607-gnosis-3-or-10-merit-points#post1069607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Low Gnosis mage is front loaded by buying &quot;advanced&quot; merits that give the benefit of 2 standard merit points per each merit point put into it (literally for mystery cult and some others). If low gnosis mage has to prioritize getting gnosis to 3 then high gnosis mage will pull even as soon as high gnosis mage accumulates 10 xp. Assuming high gnosis mage is getting 2xp per session, this should take place around session 5. Assuming low gnosis mage only gets 1.5 xp per session it will take 7 sessions to buy up Gnosis to 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth remembering that Gnosis also has a lower barrier to justifying purchases without chunks of downtime \u2014 you can manage to accomplish multiple breakthroughs in mystical insight a lot more easily than you can move up in the Caucus or track down a Familiar candidate.<br /> <br /> The Megumin build has its charms, to be sure, but characters built to interact with an inhabited setting will do better to play the long game than risk being <i>just</i> mystically potent while your seniors are mystically potent <i>and</i> sitting on a pile of favors and swag <i>and</i> ultimately capable of having their character sheets advanced at an arbitrary rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T14:33:04-07:00","id":1069624,"title":"","content":"Funny that &quot;Gnosis 2, 5 Merits&quot; is not even mentioned, but it's understandable. 10 Merits / 1 Gnosis and 3 Gnosis / 0 Merits both have their own niches, but Gnosis 2 kinda just...is. <br /> I have found out that allowing joining a Legacy in exchange for 1 or 2 Merit dots that have to come from the starting pool, not the &quot;Merit generating merits&quot;, makes it a competetive option with it's own strong points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T14:38:30-07:00","id":1069627,"title":"","content":"I think the Gnosis 3 option is being a bit over sold in terms of how the advantages actually play out, and disregarding some of the disadvantages.<br /> <br /> For example, joining a Legacy requires being allowed into one, and founding your own costs you Arcane XP (and you need to recruit members to gain a lot of the XP advantages).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T15:07:37-07:00","id":1069653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1069607-gnosis-3-or-10-merit-points?p=1069624#post1069624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny that &quot;Gnosis 2, 5 Merits&quot; is not even mentioned, but it's understandable. 10 Merits / 1 Gnosis and 3 Gnosis / 0 Merits both have their own niches, but Gnosis 2 kinda just...is.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the 2 second edition games I've run, most players have gone with Gnosis 2 just because that first expansion of spell control is so incredibly useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T15:15:29-07:00","id":1069657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1069607-gnosis-3-or-10-merit-points?p=1069612#post1069612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that some Merits can only be bought at character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But many of those merits can also be copied via arcana. Life magic should be able to give the character most only at character creation physical merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12994-steveintexas","name":"SteveInTexas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T15:24:23-07:00","id":1069664,"title":"","content":"Well, it's not a big deal for those with Life and Mind, but those mages that don't focus on those two Arcana won't be able to grant themselves similar effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T15:33:11-07:00","id":1069666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1069607-gnosis-3-or-10-merit-points?p=1069664#post1069664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's not a big deal for those with Life and Mind, but those mages that don't focus on those two Arcana won't be able to grant themselves similar effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>See also the problems of dispellation, spell control, and the related complications of each \u2014 characters will not always have the luxury of setting up secure temporary fixes with spellwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:04:19-07:00","id":1069685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1069607-gnosis-3-or-10-merit-points?p=1069627#post1069627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Gnosis 3 option is being a bit over sold in terms of how the advantages actually play out, and disregarding some of the disadvantages.<br /> <br /> For example, joining a Legacy requires being allowed into one, and founding your own costs you Arcane XP (and you need to recruit members to gain a lot of the XP advantages).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I'm confusing 1e and 2e. I thought you had to pay 1xp (arcane or normal) to join an existing legacy and learn its first attainment or 1 arcane xp to create your own legacy and learn its first attainment. I can see how this could also be read that initiation is a game event that does not required xp for an established legacy, that all attainments are optional, and that founding a legacy requires an additional arcane XP. I think this is probably wrong, but solely based on how legacies worked in 1e.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I just realized you can do something horrifically cheesy and be completely in setting. Mystery cult allows mage only merits. Setup the cabal as a mystery cult:<br /> *: Themed Cabal<br /> **, Shadow Name *<br /> ***, Shadow Name ***<br /> **** Professional Training *** Arcane Troubleshooter (Occult, Firearms and most likely Socialize as asset skills).<br /> ***** Consilium Status +***<br /> <br /> And it is actually, perfectly thematically appropriate to discover ones mystical name through initiation into a mystery cult. You can even justify the status bump. This cabal is made up of highly competent professionals who do the Mage thing hardcore.<br /> <br /> Though, bits of cheese aside, what I'm trying to get at is that Shadow name is three dots plus themed cabal that everyone is going to want to have. If you run it through a mystery cult you can use the last two levels of the cult to give six dots of merits for the price of two. That's a great way to pick up some of the classic &quot;merit tax&quot; merits such as resources. If you throw that a the Gnosis 3 character above you can get: Gnosis 4, Ruling Arcana 4, Mystery Cult Influence 4 (Shadow Name 3, Themed Cabal 1, Resources 2, Allies 1), Legacy Attainment 1, Consilium Status 1 (edit had it at 3, figured 16 not 14 xp duh) and +1 Praxis from the Gnosis bump. That seems like a powerful and influential character.<br /> <br /> Albeit you can do the same thing with the low gnosis character but the high gnosis character benefits from generating more XP to buy merits that provide extra merit dots..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12994,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12994-steveintexas","user":"SteveInTexas","date":". 03-28-2017, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12994-steveintexas","name":"SteveInTexas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:14:10-07:00","id":1069691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1069607-gnosis-3-or-10-merit-points?p=1069664#post1069664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's not a big deal for those with Life and Mind, but those mages that don't focus on those two Arcana won't be able to grant themselves similar effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>For merits or abilities:<br /> <br /> For Merits you have Life, Mind, Time, Fate and Space (create temporary attachments between yourself and others) possibly some uses of matter, plus - possibly depending on how you handle it - death and spirit (most likely for contacts or allies). Plus Prime in some instances.<br /> <br /> For Long term &quot;template additions&quot; you have life, prime, forces, possibly death (various shadow stuff), Fate (that enchant item rote)), possibly matter and hung spells with time, You might be able to do with with spirit but, yeah the shadow. <br /> <br /> Keep in mind that while Life effects are flashy, if the game does not turn on combat other forms of long term effects (such as the prime 1 see truth rote) are also candidates for long term spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12994-steveintexas","name":"SteveInTexas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:37:22-07:00","id":1069711,"title":"","content":"If you want cheese, you grab Mystery Cult, Masque at 5 and either buy more Masques, or get some Status to gain sweet sweet permanent purchases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:40:03-07:00","id":1069712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1069607-gnosis-3-or-10-merit-points?p=1069653#post1069653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the 2 second edition games I've run, most players have gone with Gnosis 2 just because that first expansion of spell control is so incredibly useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it will be a big deal too, but with surprising amount of ways to circumvent that - Sleepwalkers holding Control for you, Sanctum, no danger in unsafely relinquishing a spell that lasts less than a day - it actually end up not being felt at all. Especially when combined with the fact that 1 Reach to cast second spell isn't that harsh for people who can get 2 Reach worth of Paradox reduction from using a Dedicated Tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:52:36-07:00","id":1069717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1069607-gnosis-3-or-10-merit-points?p=1069711#post1069711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want cheese, you grab Mystery Cult, Masque at 5 and either buy more Masques, or get some Status to gain sweet sweet permanent purchases.</div> </div> </div> </div>You explicitly can't buy more Masques with the free dots from Masque.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:56:31-07:00","id":1069720,"title":"","content":"And nobody says he can? We are talking about 10 points of Merits here. Masques 5 and Mystery Cult 3 still leaves you with leftover points to spend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T17:36:35-07:00","id":1069736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1069607-gnosis-3-or-10-merit-points?p=1069720#post1069720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And nobody says he can? We are talking about 10 points of Merits here. Masques 5 and Mystery Cult 3 still leaves you with leftover points to spend.</div> </div> </div> </div>You stuck Masque 5 in the middle of a list with other Merits when Masque 5 gives you free Merit dots to spend, which is a point of confusion that could have been avoided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-28-2017, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T17:42:40-07:00","id":1069740,"title":"","content":"Always buy merits. Merits are great and create roleplaying opportunities, even if they aren't of much immediate mechanical advantage; they inform of who the character is and give your ST a chance to throw unique challenges at you as well that can be solved by invoking the character's background. Sure, five dots in Resources doesn't come up as often as a dot of Gnosis might, but your character always wearing sharp clothes or cutting cheques to get out of a problematic situation will give a deeper sense of who they are (as would them never dressing to impress despite ample chance to do so).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T17:57:17-07:00","id":1069748,"title":"","content":"I'm going to argue that permanently connecting your brain to Internet and starting to function like a human computer, turning yourself into a genetically redefined person, and other enhancements you can graft into your spell control can provide as much roleplaying opportunities as merits. Like, the very example you give - always wearing sharp clothes - is something you can achieve with more Gnosis due to having spell control up. <br /> <br /> As for Satchel - context of conversation is spending your starting 10 merit dots. I don't understand why you are blaming me for your assumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T18:24:10-07:00","id":1069763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1069607-gnosis-3-or-10-merit-points?p=1069748#post1069748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Satchel - context of conversation is spending your starting 10 merit dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>The context of the conversation is also you talking about how to &quot;cheese&quot; more Merits out of the starting 10 and then mentioning a Merit immediately after a Merit that lets you access other Merits in a fashion that looked like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/881992-mage-the-awakening-2nd-edition-errata-thread?p=891314#post891314\">a point of confusion that has happened before</a>.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't understand why you are blaming me for your assumptions. </div> </div> </div>Nobody said anything about blame. You made an ambiguous statement, I misinterpreted it, then you acted like misinterpreting it was difficult to do, and then I explained why that misinterpretation happened. There is no offensive action that takes place in this sequence of events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T18:24:52-07:00","id":1069764,"title":"","content":"One issue might be explaining why a character has no merit dots. Is she a stay at home mom? Did he or she awaken and use life magic to heal a child dying of cancer, only to have the magic cause both child and spouse to suffer a breaking point (for particular CoD gruesome -- the child then killed the spouse in a murder suicide and the spouse was found with a look of understanding on his/her face)? Is this person wanted by the police as a result of a particularly explosive mystery play? There are other tools than just merits, including spell slots, aspirations, obsessions and skills with which to shape the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12994-steveintexas","name":"SteveInTexas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T19:03:31-07:00","id":1069771,"title":"","content":"Mages who awaken via the &quot;waking world dream&quot; route routinely expend great lengths of time on the streets or in asylums as raving madmen/women during the process of awakening. That has a way of eroding your worldly influence and connections. It's entirely possible for a mage to finally awaken and find herself in a foreign country, having been declared legally dead months previously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T20:31:24-07:00","id":1069825,"title":"","content":"I like getting things. I have a whole list of 'Gifts I Want' for my werewolf. Non-Affinity Gifts cost 5 Experiences, as much as a Primal Urge, the werewolf equivalent to Gnosis, while Facets for Gifts you've already opened up just cost 2. So I wasn't exactly getting these every session but I was spending my Experiences when I gathered enough to get something from my list. And the times I had 5 or more Experiences saved up were rare.<br /> <br /> I grant this is not a problem for everyone, some people are entirely comfortable and patient playing game after game, watching the Experiences stack up and not purchasing any of those things they've wanted, or not wanting something else to begin with. It might just come up less in mage, since Gifts aren't a thing and Gnosis acts as a sort of hard limiter for Arcana.<br /> <br /> But 5 Experiences is a lot to save up for. How much people seem to get per games varies, but there's usually not more than 1 Experience gained per session, so you're looking at at least 5 sessions to pick up that Gnosis. While with the same 1 Experience per session you can pick up those Merits, the non-character creation only ones at least, piecemeal.<br /> <br /> More might depend on what the game is going to be like. If it's a short game that's going to have 1 session a week for a month, purchasing that Gnosis upgrade just won't come up. And if your game is, say, taking place isolated on a deserted island, Merit dots in Mystery Cult to represent a legion of followers might be prohibited. And, of course, a lot is going to depend on your character concept. If you get the Gnosis, figuring you can buy your Fighting Styles as the game progresses, you might not want to start with a martial artist cult leader who's a high ranking member of the Guardians of the Veil. I don't think there's an objectively better choice without taking in factors like these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T07:34:39-07:00","id":1070053,"title":"","content":"Merits that give Merits -- still the cheesiest mechanic ever.<br /> <br /> It's interesting that whenever these threads crop up, no one ever considers Chronicle length. If you're going to play a dozen sessions and move on, then Merits are going to be a better choice*. You have to play long-term for the cost benefit of Gnosis to make a difference. Flip side? Reeeeaaaally long term can also highlight the value of Creation Only merits as all characters approach singularities of power level.<br /> <br /> * The things we have and don't have tend to affect the decisions we make. We gravitate towards our better dice pools and shy away from our worse ones. The more fx you have, the more likely you are to <i>see </i>opportunities.<br /> <br /> Also, shout out to a fellow Texan !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}